{
  "id": "https://m-lancini.github.io/frida-vocab/dictionary/long-term-illness",
  "type": "Concept",
  "prefLabel": {
    "en": "long-term illness"
  },
  "definition": {
    "en": "A health condition of extended duration which may result in lasting physical or psychological impairments that affect an individual’s ability to participate fully in professional and social life."
  },
  "scopeNote": {
    "en": [
      "According to the case law of the Court of Justice of the European Union, a long-term illness may qualify as a disability where it entails long-lasting physical, mental, or psychological impairments which, in interaction with various barriers, hinder full participation in work. The Court of Justice of the European Union furthermore has increasingly clarified that the effects of long‑term health conditions must be assessed in light of the prohibition of direct and indirect discrimination and the requirement to adopt appropriate measures to ensure equal treatment"
    ]
  },
  "notation": [
    "4.8"
  ],
  "broader": {
    "id": "https://m-lancini.github.io/frida-vocab/dictionary/section-4",
    "prefLabel": {
      "en": "Disability, impairment and accessibility"
    }
  },
  "related": [
    {
      "id": "https://m-lancini.github.io/frida-vocab/dictionary/impairment",
